domain ADR0032DesignConsistencyCheck:
  description "Check the historical D11 implementation design against accepted ADR0032."
problem P1:
  |
    Identify which design clauses remain current and which cannot govern implementation
    after ADR0032 acceptance.
evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR0032 separates transport, worker, semantic-progress and cumulative
    resource controls, removes fixed whole-attempt wall clock as semantic termination,
    and leaves exact provider and worker values pending later acceptance.
evidence E2:
  |
    Design section 7.1 sets an attempt elapsed maximum of 240 seconds and one provider
    call maximum of 60 seconds, then states that all dimensions are hard maxima and the
    first exhausted dimension stops new work.
evidence E3:
  |
    Design section 7.2 requires each provider reservation's elapsed allowance to fit
    the remaining whole-attempt elapsed limit.
evidence E4:
  |
    The corrected design-acceptance record preserves revision two as a historical
    reviewed snapshot but removes activation authority from the concrete numerical
    execution policy and time-based termination semantics pending a successor ADR.
evidence E5:
  |
    The remaining design sections define typed kernel and adapter boundaries, focused
    work, protected meaning, cumulative non-time accounting, progress detection,
    persistence, fencing, owner review and separate activation authority, all retained
    by ADR0032 D5.
premise C1:
  |
    A historical reviewed snapshot may remain unchanged, but superseded clauses cannot
    be used as the current implementation specification merely because the file retains
    its old text.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, C1:
  |
    Classify the design as partially inconsistent with current authority. Section 7.1's
    240-second whole-attempt limit, 60-second provider literal and all-dimensions hard-max
    statement, plus section 7.2's whole-attempt elapsed reservation composition, are
    superseded and must be revised before implementation relies on this design.
decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E4, E5, C1:
  |
    Retain the design's non-time architecture as applicable subject to ADR0032. Do not
    classify the whole design as rejected and do not infer replacement time values.
decision D3 based_on P1, D1, D2:
  |
    Record the inconsistency without editing the historical design in this check-only
    scope. The next design revision must remove whole-attempt semantic expiry, separate
    provider and worker boundaries, preserve the other budgets, and keep exact time
    values pending their named evidence and owner decision.
